WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.500
- [George] From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.400
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.180
between Pocky in Japan and the US.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.789
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.170
In Japan, our Pocky comes in a 72-gram box

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:20.643
which contains two
packets and a nine-pack.

00:00:21.546 --> 00:00:23.260
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.740
- Our Pocky's come in
basically three sizes.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.750
The one 1.14-ounce box,
the 2.47-ounce box,

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.300
and the 4.13-ounce boxy bag.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.690
But our strawberry-flavored box is smaller

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.840
than this chocolate box.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.570
This is a 3.81-ounce box,

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.810
which is 0.32 ounces
smaller than this one.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.080
Largest box bag is this,
the Cookies &amp; Cream flavor,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.240
which is 4.57 ounces

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.230
or 0.44 grams larger
than the chocolate box.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:56.745
One theory, my theory,

00:00:56.745 --> 00:00:59.467
is that the Pocky boxes
contain a specific number

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:00.460
of Pocky sticks

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.700
and each Pocky is a different weight

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.820
based on the flavor coating.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.840
So we're gonna weigh
each Pocky individually

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.413
to see if this is true.

00:01:10.413 --> 00:01:12.730
All right, chocolate first.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:17.330
So seven of these are 13 grams.
Can someone write that down?

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:22.060
Strawberry, seven is 13 grams.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.770
Was that what the first one was? Okay.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.160
Cookies &amp; Cream!

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.380
Cookies &amp; Cream, seven
of them are 18 grams.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.800
Well, the Cookies &amp; Cream ones
are definitely a lot heavier.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.633
A lot heavier.

00:01:33.633 --> 00:01:36.610
(Joe chomping)

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:37.690
Mm!

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:40.747
- So let's see how many
Pocky are in a box.

00:01:40.747 --> 00:01:44.521
(George counting in Japanese)

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:48.284
(audio chirping)

00:01:48.284 --> 00:01:52.943
32, 33, 34.

00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:55.300
Thirty-four Pocky in total.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.550
So one packet has 17 Pocky

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.670
and another one also has 17 Pocky.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.562
- Let's see how many
Pocky's are in this box.

00:02:02.562 --> 00:02:05.392
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

00:02:05.392 --> 00:02:06.920
(exhales) Oh, man.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:10.563
Is this normal?

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:12.243
I think I can kind of like,

00:02:12.243 --> 00:02:15.480
do you wanna get a
close-up on there before?

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.486
So one, two, three, those
are the broken ones.

00:02:17.486 --> 00:02:19.210
(audio chirping)

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:24.210
30, 31, 32, 33, 34, 35, 36.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:25.560
You know how everyone
was complaining about

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.167
how I eat Kit-Kats in the Kit-Kat episode?

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:30.218
(suspenseful music)

00:02:30.218 --> 00:02:32.570
(Joe chomps)

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:34.464
(Joe chewing)

00:02:34.464 --> 00:02:36.684
Mm!

00:02:36.684 --> 00:02:38.880
(upbeat music)

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.020
Here's all the Pocky's
that are native to the US

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.720
that are not in Japan.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.880
- And here are all the
Pocky's native to Japan.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:49.370
- Cookies &amp; Cream, Cookies &amp; Cream.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:51.238
Not a solid block, so that's good.

00:02:51.238 --> 00:02:53.739
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:54.770
(Joe chomping)

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:58.400
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.960
Mm!

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:00.793
I like those.

00:03:00.793 --> 00:03:02.410
This looks like fun, Yuelei.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.340
Chocolate Banana, have
you had these before?

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.173
You have?

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.688
No, mm-mm.

00:03:07.688 --> 00:03:09.593
That banana flavor hits right away.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:12.533
Oh, no.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:14.940
Matcha green tea.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.863
Any "Food Wars" heads watching know,

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.063
Joe does not like matcha.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.954
Mm, smells like a freshly-cut lawn.

00:03:22.954 --> 00:03:23.893
(lawnmower rumbles)

00:03:23.893 --> 00:03:25.890
(Joe chomps)

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.580
Yeah, nah.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.690
There's also a Crunchy Strawberry
flavor you can get here

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:30.523
in the US,

00:03:30.523 --> 00:03:32.320
but I was not able to get my hands on it

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.900
by the time of filming this episode.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.704
So here's just regular strawberry.

00:03:38.704 --> 00:03:39.537
Uh-oh.

00:03:39.537 --> 00:03:42.990
Oh, another solid block.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:43.823
Yeah.

00:03:46.607 --> 00:03:48.316
(Joe chomps)
(audience gasps)

00:03:48.316 --> 00:03:50.658
Mm, yeah, dude.

00:03:50.658 --> 00:03:52.700
Put me in jail for crimes against Pocky's.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:54.803
- George's energy.

00:03:54.803 --> 00:03:56.883
Bong, let's go!

00:03:56.883 --> 00:03:59.360
All right, let's start with this one.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.383
We have Pocky Luxury Milk Chocolate.

00:04:04.704 --> 00:04:07.050
(laughs) Is it Pocky?

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.240
You look like corn dog.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.663
What happened to you?

00:04:12.953 --> 00:04:13.786
Hmm.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:20.250
It's got milk and fermented butter flavor.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.800
And we have another corn dog.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.262
It's a Almond Milk flavor.

00:04:25.262 --> 00:04:27.353
(George speaks in Japanese)

00:04:29.261 --> 00:04:30.820
Mm.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:33.610
It has strong almond milk flavor.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.770
I prefer this one, the milk chocolate,

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.830
but both are so short.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:39.663
You should be longer.

00:04:39.663 --> 00:04:40.610
(whistle screeches)

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:41.570
You too!

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.383
We have this ultra-thin Pocky.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.200
Oh. (laughs)

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.650
You are so thin this time.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.550
This one is short.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:54.870
This one is so thin.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.930
We have Tasty.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.470
Why is it Tasty?

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:05.533
Oh, fermented butter
is used for this stick.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:07.943
Ooh.

00:05:09.321 --> 00:05:10.910
(George chomps)

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.420
It's got just a little
bit of butter flavor.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:18.110
I still prefer this one, this corn dog.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.920
Almond Crush.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.663
It's a little different.
Look at the packets.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.600
Yeah, obviously, it's got almonds.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.068
Okey-dokey, Pocky.

00:05:29.068 --> 00:05:30.979
(George speaks in Japanese)

00:05:32.154 --> 00:05:33.154
I love this.

00:05:34.493 --> 00:05:36.851
I love this.

00:05:36.851 --> 00:05:37.853
Mm.

00:05:37.853 --> 00:05:41.090
We've got Pocky Chocolate Coconut.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:45.943
Oh, this one is also
this style of packets.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:49.240
Oh.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:52.393
It's pretty similar with
this one, Almond Crush.

00:05:53.582 --> 00:05:55.450
(George chomps)

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.720
Hmm?

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.590
Yeah, obviously, it's got coconut flavor,

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:03.070
and also, it's got a
little bit of saltiness.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:04.290
It's not my taste.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:07.057
Strawberry chocolate Pocky.

00:06:07.057 --> 00:06:09.220
(George chomps)

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.053
Oh.

00:06:11.016 --> 00:06:11.849
Ah.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:16.470
Right after you bite this,
you get some sweetness.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.610
But after that, you get sourness.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.063
It smells so strong.

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.950
I can smell it from here.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.140
Cocoa powder Pocky,

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:29.580
And it says you can only
get this in winter season.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:32.113
Oh yeah, look at this.
It's got cocoa powder.

00:06:34.871 --> 00:06:36.981
(George speaks in Japanese)

00:06:36.981 --> 00:06:38.500
(George's lips smack)

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.720
We've got the cutest Pocky ever.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.670
Cherry heart-shaped Pocky.

00:06:44.762 --> 00:06:46.178
Aha.

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:50.130
Oh, look at this!

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.130
Heart! It's in there.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.660
How cute.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:56.433
And this part, cherry
chocolate is so awesome.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.680
You get strong cherry flavor.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:03.999
We've also got blueberry
heart-shaped chocolate Pocky.

00:07:03.999 --> 00:07:05.318
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

00:07:05.318 --> 00:07:07.770
Ooh, look at this.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.220
So blue.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:13.347
This color doesn't make me want
to eat this, but let's try.

00:07:13.347 --> 00:07:15.904
(George speaks in Japanese)

00:07:15.904 --> 00:07:17.445
Ooh!

00:07:17.445 --> 00:07:18.278
Mm.

00:07:19.143 --> 00:07:20.930
So sour.

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.123
But look at this heart-shaped Pocky.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:24.873
Not for me.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:29.890
This is what I've been
waiting for, sakura matcha.

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.870
So "sakura" means cherry blossom.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.623
Cherry blossom matcha taste.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:36.773
Ooh.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.680
Look at this!

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.750
So it's got matcha chocolate

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.727
and this stick is pink.

00:07:45.727 --> 00:07:47.870
(George chomps)

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:51.730
Mm, this is so Japanese-y Pocky.

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:53.330
Just sweet matcha.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:55.796
The feeling of spring has come to my life.

00:07:55.796 --> 00:07:57.010
(bird chirping)

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:58.673
Spring days here in my body.

00:07:59.676 --> 00:08:04.638
(George sings in Japanese)

00:08:04.638 --> 00:08:07.181
Everybody's curious what these are.

00:08:07.181 --> 00:08:08.570
Megami no Ruby.

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:11.000
Otona no Kohaku.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.220
What does it mean?

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.843
I don't even know. (laughs)

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:18.273
Anyway, so it says Megami no Ruby.

00:08:18.273 --> 00:08:22.730
It means like, "Goddess Ruby".

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:26.230
Otona no Kohaku, in
English, it says, "amber."

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:30.010
Kind of like stone, fossil, jewel.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:33.185
It says it goes well with red wine.

00:08:33.185 --> 00:08:34.157
Interesting.

00:08:34.157 --> 00:08:35.917
Ta-da!

00:08:35.917 --> 00:08:38.920
It looks like regular chocolate Pocky.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.062
(George chomps)

00:08:41.062 --> 00:08:41.895
Oh?

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:43.843
What is this?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.220
This taste itself is like berries.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:51.175
This one goes well with whiskey.

00:08:51.175 --> 00:08:53.895
(George chomps)

00:08:53.895 --> 00:08:54.728
Huh?

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:59.070
It's pretty close to dark
chocolate, it's bitter.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:02.350
In Japan, we have this
Gokuboso extra-fine Pocky,

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.320
which are roughly half the thickness

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.127
of a regular chocolate Pocky.

00:09:06.127 --> 00:09:09.010
- In the US, ours are
called the Ultra Slim.

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:11.690
- I got a new digital scale.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.370
What I'm gonna do is weigh
a regular chocolate Pocky.

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:18.070
2.13 grams.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:20.230
So ultra thin Pocky.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:23.921
So it weighs 1.52 grams.

00:09:23.921 --> 00:09:26.830
- Thinner, that's it?

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:27.683
Here's a big boy.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.500
Here's the thin.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:31.637
Is it able to do this?

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:33.183
Can I get out of the way so
it's just the white background?

00:09:33.183 --> 00:09:37.980
23, 24, 25, and there's another
bag in here, so 50 per box.

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.530
Okay, so 50 instead of 36.

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:42.790
Seven regular Pocky's are 13 grams.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.830
Let's see how many slim ones
we needed to get to 13 grams.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:49.405
5, 6, 7, 8 1/2.

00:09:49.405 --> 00:09:51.597
Eight and a half slim ones are the same

00:09:51.597 --> 00:09:53.310
as seven regular ones.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.800
Is that that much slimmer?

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.150
I guess that's slimmer.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.340
Does anyone think that's
not significant enough

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.880
to be a selling point?

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:02.770
Pocky adjusts its sweetness
for different countries.

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:05.860
Not surprisingly, the US
ones are meant to be sweeter.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.950
I'm gonna do a taste test side by side.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.060
We got the American ones
and the Japanese one,

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:12.540
and we're gonna see just
how different they taste.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.000
I'm worried that these are
also gonna be a Pocky popsicle.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:16.833
Oh no, okay.

00:10:17.979 --> 00:10:19.320
Japanese.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:20.630
These are only Japanese ones I can find.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:23.832
Obviously, they're bigger. I
don't know if this is the norm.

00:10:23.832 --> 00:10:25.144
(Joe chomps)

00:10:25.144 --> 00:10:27.883
Mm-hm, in the baseline sweetness.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:33.130
Yeah.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:33.963
Mm.

00:10:35.077 --> 00:10:37.494
(Joe chomps)

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.770
Yeah, it's noticeably different.

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:46.770
They taste identical, but
ours has a sweet aftertaste.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.350
I like the Japanese ones much better.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:52.900
- So Pocky is in the Guinness
World Records three times.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.720
It's the largest
chocolate-coated biscuits brand,

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:57.640
has the most mentions of a brand name

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.970
on Twitter in 24 hours,

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.830
which was 3,710,044 times.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:05.890
And finally, it was part

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:09.030
of the most people opening
packaged food online

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:12.770
simultaneously with 143 people.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:15.020
- 143 people, that's it?

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.670
That doesn't seem like that many.

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:18.650
I feel like I've been on Zoom work calls

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:22.280
with 143 people in it, right?

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:25.100
It would've been literally
one email to set that up.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.387
- I can do (George speaks in Japanese).

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:32.440
Pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:36.860
Now I got more than 200
George's clones right here.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.880
Simultaneously, three, two, one.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:40.713
Boom.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:45.850
Now I broke the Guinness World Records.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.690
So November 11th is known as
a Pocky (speaks in Japanese)

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:50.870
or Pocky Day in Japan.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:54.420
This date was chosen because
a Pocky is shaped like a one.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:58.170
At November 11th, visually,
it looks like four Pocky.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:01.720
And also, Pretz are included
in this day, November 11th,

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:03.830
which is the pretzel version of Pocky.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:07.510
And in Japan, you can get
them in flavors like Salad,

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:12.510
Ripe Tomato, Sweet Potato,
and Roasted Bread flavor.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:14.540
In the US, we also have Pretz,

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:19.000
and we get these fun flavors
like Sweet Corn, fun,

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.979
and Pizza.

00:12:20.979 --> 00:12:22.163
Oh, God.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:25.411
It has nothing on it.

00:12:25.411 --> 00:12:26.650
(Joe chomps)

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:27.560
Nope.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:31.540
I mean, yeah, it tastes like corn.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:32.530
Why though?

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:36.531
What is the demand for
corn-flavored sticks?

00:12:36.531 --> 00:12:37.870
(Joe sighs)

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:41.170
Besides pizza, anything
flavored like pizza is terrible.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:43.177
Even pizza combos aren't very good.

00:12:43.177 --> 00:12:44.940
(Pretz wrapper crinkles)

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:45.980
No.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:48.060
(Joe chomps)

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.860
I mean, it's up there with croutons.

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:53.330
Does anyone grab a handful
of croutons on-the-go?

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.960
And would just eating a box of croutons.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.114
These probably would be good on something.

00:12:57.114 --> 00:13:00.120
(catchy music)

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:02.340
- In Japan, our chocolate Pocky box,

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.480
per 100 grams, has 506 calories.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:08.350
Adjusted for the box size, 72 grams,

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:12.910
the package contains 364.3 calories.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:16.527
And let's break it down
even further to per Pocky.

00:13:16.527 --> 00:13:21.300
One Pocky contains, on
average, 11.38 calories.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:26.270
- A US chocolate Pocky
box contains 340 calories.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:29.080
Just a little bit less
than a Japanese box,

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.970
but note, there is a two-gram difference.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:34.050
Now here at "Food Wars", we
thrive on scientific accuracy.

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:36.270
So let's break it down per Pocky.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:41.230
One US Pocky is 9.44444444444444444...

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:46.900
calories.

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:50.580
- The highest-calorie Pocky
in Japan is to be determined.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.414
We emailed the customer service,

00:13:52.414 --> 00:13:55.336
but we didn't get their response.

00:13:55.336 --> 00:13:57.423
What are you doing? Hurry up!

00:13:57.423 --> 00:14:02.423
But I guess this Pocky is
the most calorific Pocky.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.790
It's 196 calories.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:09.337
So it should be 'cause it's
got a lot of butter in it.

00:14:09.337 --> 00:14:10.700
- The US Pocky

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.750
with the most calories
is the Cookies &amp; Cream.

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:17.430
It contains total 630 calories.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:19.648
There's no question I
can murder this whole box

00:14:19.648 --> 00:14:20.910
in one sitting.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.370
630 calories? That's nothing.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:25.530
That's kind of reassuring
like, "Wow, only 630?

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:26.952
Found my breakfast!"

00:14:26.952 --> 00:14:30.020
(steady music)

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.440
- Japa-Pocky contains these ingredients.

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:36.700
Wheat flour, sugar, cacao
mass, vegetable oils,

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:40.210
whole-milk powder,
shortening, malt extract,

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:44.890
starch, salt, yeast, cocoa powder, butter,

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:49.400
emulsifier, flavoring, leavening
agent, annatto coloring,

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.960
and mineral salt.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:54.700
- Any US Pocky contains
wheat flour, sugar,

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.860
chocolate liquor, blend of vegetable oils,

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:59.710
that blend being sunflower oil, palm oil,

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.250
whole-milk powder,
vegetable oil shortening,

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:05.480
which is palm oil, hydrogenated
palm oil, and cocoa butter,

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:08.770
salt, artificial flavors,
yeast, soy lecithin,

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.680
leavening, sodium bicarbonate,

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:15.020
mono- and diglycerides of fatty acids.

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:16.490
Wink.

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:19.330
- In Japan, our Pocky
contains malt extract,

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.540
which is sometimes used as a replacement

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.020
for sugar in baking.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.903
It contains lots of maltose,

00:15:24.903 --> 00:15:26.040
a type of sugar

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.800
which actually has a
higher glycemic index value

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:30.040
than normal sucrose.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.930
So it's a surprise that
American Pocky are supposed

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.460
to be sweeter.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.660
- There are actually differences
in the types of cocoa used.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:39.250
If you've watched the "US
versus UK Snickers" episode,

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:42.490
you know that American
chocolate is not so great.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:45.440
In the US, our Pockys are
made with chocolate liquor

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:46.830
and cocoa butter.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:49.250
Chocolate liquor is just
cocoa that's been processed

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:50.560
into semisolid form,

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:54.430
and it's actually around
50% cocoa butter itself.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.890
The trouble is for an American product

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.650
to be classified as milk chocolate,

00:15:57.650 --> 00:16:01.107
it only needs to contain
around 10% of chocolate liquor,

00:16:01.107 --> 00:16:03.150
and the rest can be made up of sugars

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.850
and various ingredients.

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:06.930
- In Japan, the rules are different,

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:08.960
depending on the type of product.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.910
Milk chocolate material must contain

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:14.000
at least 21% cocoa content,

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:16.420
double the required amount in America.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:18.930
So our chocolate has more chocolate.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.453
Are you jealous of us?

00:16:20.453 --> 00:16:21.483
Come to Japan.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.580
- So if I had to go favorite flavors,

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:28.303
I'm gonna go number one, number two.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:30.670
These two Pocky.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:31.970
These are the best ones.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.113
Grab your glocky when you see two Pocky.

